111
00:07:53.847 --> 00:07:55.847
♪ Change the how, but keep the what: ♪

112
00:07:56.007 --> 00:07:59.533
♪ you change one module. (Only one!) ♪

113
00:07:59.833 --> 00:08:00.984
(narrator) Verse 3, the iceberg.

114
00:08:00.984 --> 00:08:04.985
(narrator) A leader connects the exposed tip to Interface: what callers can rely on.

115
00:08:04.985 --> 00:08:07.561
(narrator) A checkmarked note says Same promised behavior.

116
00:08:07.561 --> 00:08:12.603
(narrator) Below the waterline, turning gears give way to a yellow submarine while the tip stays fixed.

117
00:08:12.603 --> 00:08:18.412
(narrator) Three choice switches change below the water: array or hash table, cache or no cache, MongoDB or Supabase.

118
00:08:18.412 --> 00:08:20.714
(narrator) New internals must keep the same contract.

119
00:08:20.714 --> 00:08:26.304
(narrator) Then a connected cutaway shows an electricity source, the grid, a wall outlet, a charger, and a phone.

120
00:08:26.304 --> 00:08:29.428
(narrator) Solar panels at noon change to wind turbines at midnight.

121
00:08:29.428 --> 00:08:35.127
(narrator) The grid continues supplying the same voltage and frequency at the outlet, and the phone keeps charging.

122
00:08:35.127 --> 00:08:38.854
(narrator) The outlet is the interface; the plant is the hidden implementation.

123
00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.040
♪ Picture an iceberg. The tip’s the interface: ♪

124
00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.900
♪ a stable contract, what the module does. ♪

125
00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.380
♪ Under the water, the implementation: ♪

126
00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.080
♪ how the module keeps its promise. ♪

127
00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.740
♪ Change it freely, as long as the tip stays the same. ♪

128
00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.460
♪ What goes below? The choices that could change: ♪

129
00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:59.380
♪ array or hash table? Cache or no cache? ♪

130
00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:02.460
♪ Mongo or Supabase? Pick one, and hide it, ♪

131
00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:04.540
